# MCP Servers

This project configures MCP servers in `.cursor/mcp.json`:

| Server | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `laravel-boost` | Laravel app tooling |
| `firecrawl` | Web scrape / crawl / search |
| `n8n` | n8n workflows (HTTP MCP) |
| `google-ads` | Official Google Ads MCP (read) |
| `google-analytics` | Official Analytics MCP (`analytics-mcp`, read) |

## Credentials

- Never commit API keys, bearer tokens, or Google credential JSON.
- Copy `.cursor/mcp.env.example` → `.cursor/mcp.env` for local notes, then **export** the vars (or set them in the Cursor / shell environment) so `${env:...}` in `mcp.json` resolves.
- `.cursor/mcp.env` is gitignored.

## Prerequisites

- **Firecrawl**: Node/`npx` + `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`
- **n8n**: `N8N_MCP_URL` + `N8N_MCP_TOKEN`
- **Google Ads / Analytics**: `pipx`, `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`, `GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID`; Ads also needs `GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN`
- After changing MCP config or env, reload Cursor MCP servers (Settings → Tools & MCP)

## Agent usage

Prefer these MCP tools when the task involves scraping, n8n automation, Google Ads reporting, or GA4 data — discover tools with GetMcpTools before calling them.
